    },
    {
      "content": "[automatic_memory_manual]\nMemory repeat interception is automatic. For read_file, write_file, run_command, and run_check, include a stable target (path, check_id, or normalized command fingerprint) so the kernel can surface prior matching receipts before loops form. When automatic_memory_findings appear in context, use prior evidence, narrow the next action, include repeat_justification, or change strategy. query_memory remains a kernel affordance only for deliberate retrieval, not a ritual first action.",
